{
  "schema": 1,
  "id": "virtualization",
  "surface": "A 200-row grid in a 120 px viewport: PageDown and Ctrl+Arrow past the rows on screen keep the positions counting, and reading mode reads on past the viewport.",
  "group": "keyboard",
  "page": "grid",
  "criteria": ["1.3.1", "2.1.1", "4.1.2"],
  "setup": [{"spreadsheetData": [200, 3]}, {"updateSettings": {"height": 120, "colHeaders": ["Alpha", "Bravo", "Charlie"]}}, {"selectCell": [0, 0]}],
  "traversal": {"from": "read-1", "to": "read-22", "items": [["A2", "A 2"], ["A3", "A 3"], ["A4", "A 4"], ["A5", "A 5"]]},
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "page-down",
      "action": {"press": "PageDown"},
      "expect": [],
      "note": "PageDown moves the selection one viewport down, past the rows a user saw: the cell it lands on and its row position."
    },
    {
      "id": "page-down-again",
      "action": {"press": "PageDown"},
      "expect": [],
      "note": "A second PageDown, into rows the grid rendered only after the first one scrolled."
    },
    {
      "id": "to-last-row",
      "action": {"press": "ControlOrMeta+ArrowDown"},
      "expect": [["a200", "a 200"], ["row 201"]],
      "note": "Ctrl+ArrowDown (Cmd on macOS) jumps to the last of the 200 rows, which the grid renders only once it scrolls there: its value and its position, which keeps counting past the rows on screen (row 201 counts the header row)."
    },
    {
      "id": "arrow-up",
      "action": {"press": "ArrowUp"},
      "expect": [["a199", "a 199"], ["row 200"]]
    },
    {
      "id": "to-first-row",
      "action": {"press": "ControlOrMeta+ArrowUp"},
      "expect": [["a1", "a 1"], ["row 2"]],
      "note": "Ctrl+ArrowUp (Cmd on macOS) jumps back to the first row, where the reading below starts."
    },
    {
      "id": "read-1",
      "action": {"read": "next"},
      "expect": [],
      "note": "The reading cursor moves on from the focused first cell, cell by cell (VoiceOver) or line by line (NVDA), past the rows the 120 px viewport shows. The traversal asks for the first column of rows 2 to 5, each once: a row the grid did not render is missing from what a reader can read, the virtualization limit."
    },
    {
